row('PV-ROW-06', D, 'All three info icons exist and carry the spec\'s VERBATIM descriptions (Units Sold and Demand always on; the Turns icon appears only once that column is enabled, with "How many times you sell through this part in a year. Higher is better."). The build\'s header label is "Turns/Yr" with no spaces; the spec and our case write "Turns / Yr". OUR WORDING must change.', E_PVUI, RC_STD, f_expected='EDIT', f_title='OK')
row('PV-ROW-07', D, 'At 1680px a 62-character description ("WHEEL BEARING GREASE, RED - HIGH TEMP (PRIMGHT64, WOIPR127651)") renders in FULL: computed text-overflow is "clip" (not ellipsis), scrollWidth equals clientWidth, and the cell carries NO title attribute, so there is no native hover tooltip. SPEC S3-R7 (verbatim): "The Description, Category, and Vendor columns truncate long text with an ellipsis on screen; the full value is available on native hover (browser tooltip)". The "Part # is never truncated" half passes. Read as a build defect. Honest limit: measured at 1680x1050; a 900px re-measure did not render a row in time.',
    E_PVUI, 'Re-measure at a narrow viewport once the branch is final.')
row('PV-ROW-08', P, 'Across ALL 10,064 rows Revenue, Margin, Units Sold, Units Returned, Sold (WO), Sold (Parts Sale) and Demand are never null; the em-dash appears only in On Hand, Turns/Yr, Min, Max, Unit Cost, Sell Price, Margin % and Last Sale (6,478 rows have a null Last Sale).', E_CALC, RC_STD)
row('PV-ROW-09', P, 'Whole-population check over all 10,064 rows: ZERO inventory rows have Units Sold 0 AND under one on hand AND zero revenue. Rows kept purely by revenue exist (e.g. 5-3256X: 0 sold, 0 on hand, $173.72). A seeded part with 5 on hand and no activity at all correctly APPEARED.', E_CALC + '; ' + E_CORE, RC_STD)
row('PV-ROW-10', P, 'CHHD2436 shows Demand 4 with Units Sold 0.00 while holding 1 on hand and $167.04 revenue; negative-movement rows exist (1221-308 at -24.00) and render with a leading minus.', E_CALC, RC_STD)
