row('PV-CALC-06', P, 'A fully-reversed in-window sale keeps its Demand count: CHHD2436 shows Demand 4 with Units Sold 0.00, and 1221-308 shows Demand 1 with Units Sold -24.00 - the reversal neither adds to nor subtracts from Demand.', E_CALC, RC_STD)
row('PV-CALC-07', P, 'In a FOUR-day This-Month window rows report Last Sale values of 573 and 574 days with Units Sold 0 and Demand 0 - Last Sale is measured over all-time history and is not clipped to the selected range; it renders "N days" and em-dash when there is no sale.', E_XTRA, RC_STD)
row('PV-CALC-08', P, 'On Hand is the row\'s own location stock, never summed: part 2750 shows 1 at Heavy Duty and 2 at Lethbridge; Min/Max are likewise per row and are read-only display columns.', E_CALC, RC_STD)
row('PV-CALC-09', D, 'Turns/Yr annualises the in-window rate and is 0.00 at zero on hand and negative when Units Sold is negative - but the WINDOW DIVISOR IS ONE DAY SHORT. BRAKECLEAN (512 sold, 618 on hand, Jan 1 - Aug 4) returns 1.40648754422, which is exactly 512/215*365/618; the spec\'s inclusive window (216 days) gives 1.39998. Reproduced on a second row (50.78875968992 = 359/215*365/12). SPEC S5 Definitions (verbatim): "Window - the whole-day span of the selected range, inclusive of both the start and end dates, with a floor of 1 day". Read as a build defect (an off-by-one in the divisor).', E_CALC, RC_STD)
